WEBVTT

00:00.372 --> 00:01.873
- [Voiceover] What I hope
to do in this video is,

00:01.873 --> 00:03.743
start with a exponential expression

00:03.743 --> 00:05.916
that's in a fairly straightforward form

00:05.916 --> 00:08.944
and then turn it into
one in a hairier form.

00:08.944 --> 00:10.370
And let's actually just do it.

00:10.370 --> 00:11.994
I'll show the initial expression

00:11.994 --> 00:14.597
and then the form that I want
it in, or that we want it in.

00:14.597 --> 00:15.797
And then we can talk a little bit about,

00:15.797 --> 00:18.085
why would ever actually wanna do that?

00:18.085 --> 00:22.311
So let's say my expression is 1/32

00:22.311 --> 00:25.136
times two to the t power.

00:25.136 --> 00:28.266
So this is fairly straightforward
exponential expression.

00:28.266 --> 00:30.094
But let's say we want it,

00:30.094 --> 00:32.613
we want it in the form

00:32.613 --> 00:35.274
A time B,

00:35.274 --> 00:36.697
and this is where it's gonna get hairy,

00:36.697 --> 00:40.577
A time B to the t over 10 power,

00:40.577 --> 00:42.506
minus one.

00:42.506 --> 00:44.112
And so, you're probably
immediately saying,

00:44.112 --> 00:45.555
"Why would I ever wanna take something

00:45.555 --> 00:47.301
"nice and simple like this

00:47.301 --> 00:50.244
"and turn it into this beastly
thing right over here?"

00:50.244 --> 00:52.457
And the answer is, when
you get into higher math

00:52.457 --> 00:54.550
and you start doing your
physics and your chemistry,

00:54.550 --> 00:56.013
you're going to see, maybe, you know,

00:56.013 --> 00:57.296
you got a result like this,

00:57.296 --> 00:58.391
but then you look in your textbook,

00:58.391 --> 01:00.727
or your professor, it
has a result like this.

01:00.727 --> 01:03.064
Just wanna know, "How do I
transfer from this to this?"

01:03.064 --> 01:05.521
Or actually, sometimes when you transfer

01:05.521 --> 01:06.557
to a form like this ...

01:06.557 --> 01:09.178
Obviously, I've just arbitrarily
written this form here.

01:09.178 --> 01:10.764
But sometimes when you write it

01:10.764 --> 01:13.060
in another form that might
even be a little hairier,

01:13.060 --> 01:16.595
it can give you an intuition
on the underlying processes

01:16.595 --> 01:19.987
that that expression
is trying to describe.

01:19.987 --> 01:22.141
So if you can take that
on a leap of faith,

01:22.141 --> 01:23.197
let's actually try to do it.

01:23.197 --> 01:24.843
And, at a minimum, it's
gonna make you a lot better

01:24.843 --> 01:26.774
at exponent properties.

01:26.774 --> 01:29.949
So see if you can rewrite
this in this form.

01:30.625 --> 01:32.290
So I'm assuming you took a go at it.

01:32.290 --> 01:33.793
So let's try to do it together.

01:33.793 --> 01:36.069
So the first thing,

01:36.069 --> 01:40.849
the first thing that I might wanna do is,

01:40.849 --> 01:42.698
well, let's see if we can ...

01:42.698 --> 01:44.648
Let's see. What would I wanna do?

01:44.648 --> 01:46.578
The first thing I wanna do is,

01:46.578 --> 01:51.064
take this t and get it into a t ...

01:51.064 --> 01:53.987
let's get it into a t over 10.

01:53.987 --> 01:55.551
So, to do that,

01:55.551 --> 01:57.705
we essentially just need to multiply by 10

01:57.705 --> 01:59.168
and divide by 10.

01:59.168 --> 02:02.175
So let's multiply by 10,

02:02.175 --> 02:04.552
and then also divide by 10.

02:04.552 --> 02:07.254
Then we haven't changed the value up here.

02:07.254 --> 02:09.428
So we can rewrite this,

02:09.428 --> 02:11.414
we can rewrite this as

02:12.069 --> 02:15.022
1/32

02:15.022 --> 02:19.110
times two

02:19.110 --> 02:20.402
to the ...

02:20.402 --> 02:23.512
So let me circle t ...

02:23.512 --> 02:25.258
Do this in a different color.

02:25.258 --> 02:30.235
T over 10,

02:30.235 --> 02:32.553
t over 10

02:32.553 --> 02:34.503
times 10.

02:34.503 --> 02:38.405
Times 10.

02:38.405 --> 02:39.643
All right. So we got a

02:39.643 --> 02:42.732
t over 10 over here.

02:42.732 --> 02:44.397
But then I have this times 10.

02:44.397 --> 02:46.856
So how do I deal with this?

02:46.856 --> 02:48.238
Well, one thing that I can do ...

02:48.238 --> 02:50.269
Let me actually just write
this the other way around.

02:50.269 --> 02:51.793
Let me write it as,

02:51.793 --> 02:53.621
let me write it as

02:53.621 --> 02:57.117
10 times t over 10.

02:57.117 --> 02:59.249
10 times

02:59.249 --> 03:01.404
t over 10.

03:01.404 --> 03:02.967
So hopefully what I just did here

03:02.967 --> 03:04.207
isn't a huge stretch here.

03:04.207 --> 03:06.990
I just literally multiplied and divide by,

03:06.990 --> 03:09.021
divided by 10, times this t over 10.

03:09.021 --> 03:10.688
But when I write it this way,

03:10.688 --> 03:13.024
an exponent property
might jump out at you.

03:13.024 --> 03:15.665
If I have, if I have

03:15.665 --> 03:17.271
a to the b,

03:17.271 --> 03:19.163
and then I raise that to the c,

03:19.163 --> 03:20.301
that's going to be a

03:20.301 --> 03:22.211
to the bc.

03:22.211 --> 03:23.116
Or, another way around,

03:23.116 --> 03:25.169
a to the bc is going to be a to the b

03:25.169 --> 03:27.281
to the c.

03:27.281 --> 03:30.817
And so, this piece right over here,

03:30.817 --> 03:32.585
I can rewrite it as

03:32.585 --> 03:34.311
two to the 10th,

03:34.311 --> 03:35.988
and then raise that

03:35.988 --> 03:38.832
to the t over 10 power.

03:38.832 --> 03:42.001
To the t over 10 power.

03:42.001 --> 03:42.997
Once again, two to the 10th

03:42.997 --> 03:44.745
and then raise that to the t over 10,

03:44.745 --> 03:45.943
that's gonna be the same thing

03:45.943 --> 03:49.457
as two to the 10 times t over 10.

03:49.457 --> 03:52.728
And of course, we still have
the one over 32 over here.

03:52.728 --> 03:55.208
One over,

03:55.208 --> 03:56.955
one over 32.

03:56.955 --> 03:58.012
I'm tempted to write that

03:58.012 --> 04:00.309
as two to the negative fifth power,

04:00.309 --> 04:02.543
but I won't do that just yet.

04:02.543 --> 04:05.063
So let's see. What's
two to the 10th power?

04:05.063 --> 04:06.810
Actually, let's just, let's just keep it,

04:06.810 --> 04:08.820
let's just keep it as
two to the 10th power,

04:08.820 --> 04:10.202
just for simplicity right now.

04:10.202 --> 04:11.154
Later we can,

04:11.154 --> 04:13.553
you might know that that's gonna be 1,024.

04:13.553 --> 04:15.682
But let's just, let's
see what else we can do.

04:15.682 --> 04:17.764
So we know this is going
to be some num- ...

04:17.764 --> 04:19.876
Actually, let me just write out as 1,024.

04:19.876 --> 04:22.070
So we have one over 32

04:22.070 --> 04:26.256
times 1,024

04:26.256 --> 04:28.571
to the t over 10,

04:28.571 --> 04:30.585
to the t over 10 power.

04:30.585 --> 04:31.883
So it seems like we're getting close.

04:31.883 --> 04:34.495
If there was no minus one here,

04:34.495 --> 04:35.958
we're essentially done.

04:35.958 --> 04:37.258
But now there's this minus one.

04:37.258 --> 04:38.977
So how do we deal with that?

04:38.977 --> 04:41.273
Well, we can do a
similar type of strategy.

04:41.273 --> 04:42.999
We can subtract one,

04:42.999 --> 04:44.930
and then we could add,

04:44.930 --> 04:46.250
and then we could add one.

04:46.250 --> 04:47.895
Then we're not actually
changing the value.

04:47.895 --> 04:50.090
Just as we multiplied
by 10 and divide by 10,

04:50.090 --> 04:51.797
we're not changing the value up here.

04:51.797 --> 04:53.829
If you subtract one and
add one to the exponent,

04:53.829 --> 04:55.859
you're not changing its value.

04:55.859 --> 04:57.546
And so, what is this going to be?

04:57.546 --> 04:59.699
We wanna leave this minus one here.

04:59.699 --> 05:01.427
But we wanna get rid of,

05:01.427 --> 05:04.189
we wanna get rid of this plus one somehow.

05:04.189 --> 05:06.404
And here, we just have to remind ourselves

05:06.404 --> 05:09.656
that, if we have a to the b

05:09.656 --> 05:13.131
times a to the c,

05:13.131 --> 05:14.430
that's going to be equal to

05:14.430 --> 05:16.827
a to the b plus c.

05:16.827 --> 05:19.298
If you have the same base, multiplied,

05:19.298 --> 05:21.235
same base raised to different exponents

05:21.235 --> 05:22.109
and you multiply them,

05:22.109 --> 05:23.857
you could just add the exponents.

05:23.857 --> 05:25.502
And so you could also
go the other way around.

05:25.502 --> 05:27.472
If you have a to the b plus c,

05:27.472 --> 05:29.138
you could break it up into a to the b

05:29.138 --> 05:31.048
times a to the c.

05:31.048 --> 05:34.096
So, this business right over here,

05:34.096 --> 05:36.005
this business right over here,

05:36.005 --> 05:38.603
this is 1,024 to the

05:38.603 --> 05:40.407
t over 10 minus one,

05:40.407 --> 05:42.298
plus one.

05:42.298 --> 05:44.431
So we can break this up as,

05:44.431 --> 05:46.544
we can break this up as,

05:46.544 --> 05:48.169
1,024,

05:48.169 --> 05:51.390
1,024 to the t

05:51.390 --> 05:53.748
over 10 minus one,

05:53.748 --> 05:55.210
that's this part here,

05:55.210 --> 05:58.013
and then times 1,024 to the one.

05:58.013 --> 05:59.090
Times ...

05:59.090 --> 06:00.654
Let me make this in a different color.

06:00.654 --> 06:02.930
So, let's see green.

06:02.930 --> 06:04.048
So this right over here.

06:04.048 --> 06:07.847
So times 1,024

06:07.847 --> 06:09.309
to the one power.

06:09.309 --> 06:11.463
That's this one power right over here.

06:11.463 --> 06:13.068
And of course, we still have

06:13.068 --> 06:14.816
the one over,

06:14.816 --> 06:17.091
the one over 32.

06:17.091 --> 06:18.533
All right. So now we're really close.

06:18.533 --> 06:21.007
We have the 1,024 to
the t over 10 minus one,

06:21.007 --> 06:22.676
we have t over 10 minus 1.

06:22.676 --> 06:24.340
And now we just have to simplify.

06:24.340 --> 06:25.132
We can rewrite.

06:25.132 --> 06:26.718
This is going to be equal to,

06:26.718 --> 06:28.098
this is going to be equal to,

06:28.098 --> 06:29.845
we can just bring the 1,024,

06:29.845 --> 06:32.102
1,024 to the first
power, that's just 1,024.

06:32.102 --> 06:35.593
So that's going to be 1,024

06:35.595 --> 06:37.038
over ...

06:37.038 --> 06:39.009
I can put all these commas here if I like.

06:39.009 --> 06:42.317
1,024 over this 32.

06:42.317 --> 06:45.038
Let me do that magenta color.

06:45.038 --> 06:47.334
Over this 32

06:47.334 --> 06:48.776
times ...

06:48.776 --> 06:49.955
home stretch.

06:49.955 --> 06:51.438
Times,

06:51.438 --> 06:54.790
times 1,024

06:54.790 --> 06:56.946
to the t over,

06:56.946 --> 06:59.464
to the t over 10

06:59.464 --> 07:01.048
minus one power.

07:01.048 --> 07:02.999
And now we could just simplify this.

07:02.999 --> 07:05.010
You might recognize 1,024,

07:05.010 --> 07:06.321
we already saw, that was the same thing

07:06.321 --> 07:08.070
as two to the 10th power.

07:08.070 --> 07:12.396
32 is the same thing as
two to the fifth power.

07:12.396 --> 07:14.967
So two to the 10th divided
by two to the fifth ...

07:14.967 --> 07:17.467
Actually, this is another
exponent property at play here,

07:17.467 --> 07:19.214
although you could just
divide the numbers.

07:19.214 --> 07:22.139
If you have a to the b

07:22.139 --> 07:23.440
over a to the c,

07:23.440 --> 07:24.579
this is going to be equal to

07:24.579 --> 07:27.240
a to the b minus c.

07:27.240 --> 07:28.234
So this is going to be

07:28.234 --> 07:30.206
two to the 10 minus five,

07:30.206 --> 07:32.268
over this whole thing.

07:32.268 --> 07:34.525
This whole thing right over here.

07:34.525 --> 07:35.805
And this thing ...

07:35.805 --> 07:37.572
See, I wanted to do that
in a different color ...

07:37.572 --> 07:39.645
This thing is just

07:39.645 --> 07:42.245
going to be two to the fifth power,

07:42.245 --> 07:43.483
or 32.

07:43.483 --> 07:45.231
So this is going to be 32

07:45.231 --> 07:47.618
times 1,024.

07:48.811 --> 07:51.016
We were in the home stretch here.

07:51.016 --> 07:53.819
1,024

07:53.819 --> 07:56.765
to the t over 10 minus one.

07:56.765 --> 07:57.740
So once again,

07:57.740 --> 07:59.002
normally in our lives,

07:59.002 --> 08:00.544
we like to make things simpler,

08:00.544 --> 08:01.986
and I'm a big advocate of that.

08:01.986 --> 08:03.390
It's a good life philosophy.

08:03.390 --> 08:04.974
But this is a case where we really did

08:04.974 --> 08:06.112
make it more complicated.

08:06.112 --> 08:07.939
We started with 1/32

08:07.939 --> 08:09.850
times two to the t ...

08:09.850 --> 08:10.624
Actually, we could have ...

08:10.624 --> 08:12.166
Well, there's other ways we
could have written that ...

08:12.166 --> 08:13.404
And we turned it into this thing

08:13.404 --> 08:15.498
with this somewhat hairier exponent.

08:15.498 --> 08:17.347
But it's a useful skill to have

08:17.347 --> 08:19.276
because you might get a result like

08:19.276 --> 08:20.477
what we originally started with,

08:20.477 --> 08:22.792
and then someone else might
get a result like this,

08:22.792 --> 08:23.725
and it's very important to realize,

08:23.725 --> 08:25.669
"Hey, you actually go the same result.

08:25.669 --> 08:27.132
"They're just different ways of expressing

08:27.132 --> 08:30.208
"the same exponential expression."
